  "title": "Break the Clustering Illusion",
  "description": "Train yourself to spot when you're overestimating the importance of random patterns or streaks. Here’s how: - Step back: Ask, “Is this pattern meaningful or could it be random?” - Check the data size: Patterns in small samples are often misleading—look for larger trends. - Seek expert advice: For complex data, consult someone with statistical expertise to avoid jumping to conclusions. Example: If you see a streak of good or bad luck, remind yourself that random events can cluster together without meaning anything.",
